script:pre-request {
  // Folders can be run on their own.
  //
  // A folder run does not replay the login in folder 1, so anything needing a
  // JWT or an API key would fail with 401. This fetches them once, on demand,
  // which makes the order in the sidebar a suggestion rather than a rule.
  //
  // Wrapped: if the runtime has no axios, every request still works when the
  // folders are run in order.
  const wantsJwt = String(req.getHeader('Authorization') || '').includes('{{jwt}}');
  const wantsKey = !!req.getHeader('X-API-Key');

  if (!wantsJwt && !wantsKey) return;

  try {
    const axios = require('axios');
    const core = bru.getEnvVar('core');

    if (!bru.getVar('jwt')) {
      const r = await axios.post(core + '/auth/login', {
        username: bru.getEnvVar('admin_user'),
        password: bru.getEnvVar('admin_password'),
      });
      bru.setVar('jwt', r.data.access_token);
      if (r.data.refresh_token) bru.setVar('refresh_token', r.data.refresh_token);
    }

    if (wantsKey && !bru.getVar('api_key')) {
      const r = await axios.post(core + '/admin/api-keys', { name: 'bruno-auto' },
        { headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + bru.getVar('jwt') } });
      bru.setVar('api_key', r.data.api_key || r.data.key);
      if (r.data.id) bru.setVar('api_key_id', r.data.id);
    }
  } catch (e) {
    console.log('auto-auth skipped:', e.message);
  }
}

docs {
  # SOC AI — every endpoint

  Run **1. Core API → Login** first: it stores the JWT, and
  **API keys → create** stores the key the SOAR requests use. A collection-level
  script fetches both on demand, so a single folder can also be run on its own.

  Requests named *(must fail)* assert a guard. A pass there means the guard held.

  The MCP connectors publish no port. Either add a `ports:` mapping while
  testing, or run from inside `soc-ai_soc-network` — see the `docker` environment.
}
